interpretation of \emph{δℓ}is more complicated. For instance, even in
Design 2 (\emph{Dg,t} = 1\emph{\{Eg ≥t ≥Fg\}}), for all \emph{g} such
that \emph{Fg −}1 + \emph{ℓ\textgreater{} Eg}, group \emph{g} has exited
the treatment at \emph{Fg −}1 + \emph{ℓ}, and

