\emph{δg,ℓ}can be estimated goes to infinity almost surely (a.s.) as
\emph{G} tends to infinity.

\textbf{Assumption 4} \emph{(Independent groups) Conditional on}
(\emph{\textbf{D}g})\emph{g≥}1\emph{, the vectors}
(\emph{\textbf{Y}g})\emph{g≥}1 \emph{are mu-tually independent.}

