\begin{quote}
\textbf{4.1} \textbf{TWFE regressions with treatment intensity
interacted with}

\textbf{period FEs.}

\textbf{Designs with variation in treatment intensity and no variation
in timing.} Among the nine papers in our census that do not have a
binary and staggered design and estimate dynamic effects, some are such
that \emph{Dg,t} = \emph{Ig}1\emph{\{t ≥F\}}, for 2 \emph{≤F ≤T}, a
special case of Design 3 where groups all start getting treated at the
same date \emph{F} with group-specific intensities \emph{Ig}, where
\emph{Ig} may be equal to zero if there are control groups that remain
completely untreated. In such designs, researchers often estimate the
following TWFE regression.

