\textbf{I}g,ℓ})\emph{−Yg,F−}1+\emph{ℓ}(\textbf{0}\emph{F−}1+\emph{ℓ})\emph{\textbar{}\textbf{D}}),
the effect of having received \emph{Ig} rather than 0 units of treatment
for \emph{ℓ}periods. Let ¯\emph{I} = (1\emph{/G})\emph{G g}=1\emph{Ig.}

