0\emph{.}294, and weights on effects of other lengths of exposure sum to
0\emph{.}648. \emph{βlp,}2 is a weighted sum of 7,626 effects, where
4,424 effects are weighted positively and 3,202 effects are weighted
negatively, and where positive and negative weights sum to 1\emph{.}085
and \emph{−}0\emph{.}584. As in Point 3 of Proposition 2, and even
though the design is not binary and staggered, the weights sum to
strictly less than one, and they actually sum to much less than one.
Then, even if \emph{δg,k/}¯\emph{Dg,k} did not vary across \emph{g} or
\emph{k},\emph{βlp,}2 would be severely biased towards zero.
\emph{βlp,}2 is contaminated by effects of other lengths of exposure
than two years. Most of those effects are weighted positively, except
for the effects of one year of exposure, whose weights sum to
\emph{−}0\emph{.}472. Intuitively, this is due to the fact that groups
with \emph{Dg,t} = 0\emph{, Dg,t}+1 \emph{\textgreater{}} 0 are used as
``control groups''
