\textbf{1.3} \textbf{Allowing for group-specific linear trends}

\textbf{Identifying assumption.} To allow for group-specific linear
trends, we replace Assumption 2 by the following assumption.

\textbf{Assumption 8} \emph{(Parallel trends for the first-differenced
status-quo outcome, conditional on the period-one treatment) ∀}(\emph{g,
g′})\emph{, if Dg,}1 = \emph{Dg′,}1 \emph{∈Dr} 1\emph{, then ∀t
≥}3\emph{,}

\begin{quote}
\emph{E}{[}\emph{Yg,t}(\emph{\textbf{D}g,}1\emph{,t})
\emph{−Yg,t−}1(\emph{\textbf{D}g,}1\emph{,t−}1)
\emph{−}(\emph{Yg,t−}1(\emph{\textbf{D}g,}1\emph{,t−}1)
\emph{−Yg,t−}2(\emph{\textbf{D}g,}1\emph{,t−}2)\emph{\textbar{}\textbf{D}}{]}
=\emph{E}{[}\emph{Yg′,t}(\emph{\textbf{D}g′,}1\emph{,t})
\emph{−Yg′,t−}1(\emph{\textbf{D}g′,}1\emph{,t−}1)
\emph{−}(\emph{Yg′,t−}1(\emph{\textbf{D}g′,}1\emph{,t−}1)
\emph{−Yg′,t−}2(\emph{\textbf{D}g′,}1\emph{,t−}2)\emph{\textbar{}\textbf{D}}{]}\emph{.}
\end{quote}

Assumption 8 is a parallel trends assumption on groups'
first-differenced status-quo outcomes, under which groups may have
different first-differenced outcome, provided groups with the same
baseline treatment all have the same expected second-differenced
outcome. Mora and Reggio (2019) already considered Assumption 8 in
designs with a binary treatment and no variation in timing. Assumption 8
extends their assumption to the designs we consider here.

